IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 266 (piece dg8, lines 1349 to 1370):
-- conversion of a domestic corporation to other entities.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online, made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation that is converting to another entity:
-- a director who must adopt the resolution, a stockholder who must be given notice and may vote, a stockholder who would
-- become a general partner. The seat layer dg8-seat.l4 asks these rules from that side.
--
-- What the section leaves to law outside this module is an input, named for the fact with its section, and listed in NOTES.md:
--   * execution, filing and the effective time of an instrument: section 103 (piece dg1); the fees prescribed under the title: section 391 (piece dg11);
--   * the fee for service on the Secretary of State: section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11); appraisal proceedings: section 262 (piece dg7);
--   * the law of the jurisdiction of the entity to which the corporation converts: not among the inputs.
-- Section 114(a) reads "stockholder" as "member" and "board of directors" as "governing body" for a nonstock corporation; section 266 is not among the sections
-- section 114(b) and (c) take out of that reading, so "stockholder" below includes a member of a nonstock corporation.

§ `s 266(a) The entities a corporation may convert to`

-- A corporation of this State may, upon the authorization of the conversion in accordance with the section, convert to a limited liability company, statutory trust,
-- business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or any other unincorporated business including a partnership, or a foreign corporation.
-- The list is read as closed (fork F12). A natural person is not an entity; a corporation of this State is not a foreign corporation (core rule, section 371(a)).
-- src:1350 | (a) A corporation of this State may, upon the authorization of such conversion in accordance with this section, convert to a limited liability company, statutory trust, business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or any other unincorporated business including a partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)) or a foreign corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(a) (src:1350)
GIVEN target IS AN Entity
      `the conversion has been authorized in accordance with the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(a) the corporation may convert to the entity` MEANS
        `the conversion has been authorized in accordance with the section`
    AND (CONSIDER target's `kind of entity`
         WHEN `a natural person` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `a corporation` kk THEN `the entity was formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` target
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

§ `s 266(b) The resolution of the board, notice to the stockholders and their vote`

-- The board adopts a resolution approving the conversion, specifying the type of entity into which the corporation shall be converted and recommending the
-- approval of the conversion by the stockholders; a plan of conversion to be adopted under (l) is approved together with the resolution.
-- src:1351 | The board of directors of the corporation which desires to convert under this section shall adopt a resolution approving such conversion, specifying the type of entity into which the corporation shall be converted and recommending the approval of such conversion by the stockholders of the corporation. If a plan of conversion is to be adopted in accordance with subsection (l) of this section, such plan shall be approved together with the resolution approving the conversion. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the board of directors adopted a resolution approving the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution specifies the type of entity into which the corporation shall be converted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution recommends the approval of the conversion by the stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a plan of conversion is to be adopted in accordance with subsection (l)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan was approved together with the resolution approving the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) the board of directors has adopted the resolution the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the board of directors adopted a resolution approving the conversion`
    AND `the resolution specifies the type of entity into which the corporation shall be converted`
    AND `the resolution recommends the approval of the conversion by the stockholders`
    AND (   (NOT `a plan of conversion is to be adopted in accordance with subsection (l)`)
         OR `the plan was approved together with the resolution approving the conversion`)

-- Due notice goes to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting: the stockholder's side of the same relation is the right to the notice.
-- src:1351 | Due notice of the time, and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the person holds stock of the corporation, voting or nonvoting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) the holder of stock is entitled to due notice of the meeting` MEANS
    `the person holds stock of the corporation, voting or nonvoting`

-- The notice states the time and purpose of the meeting, goes to the stockholder's address as it appears on the corporation's records, and is given at least 20 days
-- before the date of the meeting. "At least 20 days prior" is read inclusively: notice on the 20th day before the meeting is in time (core fork F3).
-- src:1351 | Due notice of the time, and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the notice states the time and purpose of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was sent to the stockholder at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the records of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) notice of the meeting was given to the holder as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the notice states the time and purpose of the meeting`
    AND `the notice was sent to the stockholder at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the records of the corporation`
    AND `the date on which the notice was given` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 20) `before` `the date of the meeting`)

-- The resolution is submitted to the stockholders at an annual or special meeting, where it is considered and a vote taken.
-- src:1351 | Such resolution shall be submitted to the stockholders of the corporation at an annual or special meeting. Due notice of the time, and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. At the meeting, the resolution shall be considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the resolution was submitted to the stockholders at an annual or special meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) the resolution was put to the stockholders as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the resolution was submitted to the stockholders at an annual or special meeting`
    AND `the resolution was considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection at the meeting`

-- "If a majority of the outstanding shares of stock of the corporation, entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of the resolution, the conversion shall be authorized".
-- A majority is more than half (core fork F4), counted in votes (core fork F5). NOTHING when the counts cannot be a vote (the core's rule).
-- src:1351 | If a majority of the outstanding shares of stock of the corporation, entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of the resolution, the conversion shall be authorized, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) the vote of the stockholders carries the resolution` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`

-- The proviso: if the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners, authorization also requires the approval of each stockholder who will
-- become a general partner of it as a result of the conversion. The stockholder's side: such a stockholder must approve.
-- src:1351 | provided that, if the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners, then, in addition to the foregoing approval, authorization of the conversion shall require approval of each stockholder of the corporation who will become a general partner of such partnership as a result of the conversion.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result of the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) the stockholder must approve the conversion` MEANS
        `the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners`
    AND `the stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result of the conversion`

-- The conversion is authorized when the board has adopted the resolution and the stockholders have voted for it by a majority (unless subsection (i) removes the vote:
-- no shares issued before the board adopted the resolution), and, for a conversion to a partnership with general partners, each stockholder who will become a general
-- partner has approved. NOTHING when the counts cannot be a vote.
-- src:1351 | If a majority of the outstanding shares of stock of the corporation, entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of the resolution, the conversion shall be authorized, provided that, if the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners, then, in addition to the foregoing approval, authorization of the conversion shall require approval of each stockholder of the corporation who will become a general partner of such partnership as a result of the conversion.
-- src:1366 | (i) No vote of stockholders of a corporation shall be necessary to authorize a conversion if no shares of the stock of such corporation shall have been issued prior to the adoption by the board of directors of the resolution approving the conversion.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b) (src:1351); § 266(i) (src:1366)
GIVEN `the board of directors adopted the resolution the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no shares of the stock of the corporation had been issued before the board of directors adopted the resolution approving the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result of the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each such stockholder has approved the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266(b) the conversion is authorized by the board and the stockholders` MEANS
    IF `no shares of the stock of the corporation had been issued before the board of directors adopted the resolution approving the conversion`
    THEN JUST `the board of directors adopted the resolution the subsection requires`
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 266(b) the vote of the stockholders carries the resolution` `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST carried THEN JUST (    `the board of directors adopted the resolution the subsection requires`
                                      AND carried
                                      AND (   (NOT (`the corporation is converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners` AND `a stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result of the conversion`))
                                           OR `each such stockholder has approved the conversion`))

