§ `s 266(c) Conversion to an entity of another jurisdiction: the certificate of conversion`

-- If a corporation converts to another entity organized, formed or created under the laws of a jurisdiction other than the State of Delaware, it shall file with the Secretary of State
-- a certificate of conversion executed in accordance with section 103 (piece dg1: an input).
-- src:1353 | (c) If a corporation shall convert in accordance with this section to another entity organized, formed or created under the laws of a jurisdiction other than the State of Delaware, the corporation shall file with the Secretary of State a certificate of conversion executed in accordance with § 103 of this title, which certifies:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c) (src:1353)
GIVEN `the entity to which the corporation converts is organized, formed or created under the laws of a jurisdiction other than the State of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(c) the corporation must file a certificate of conversion with the Secretary of State` MEANS
    `the entity to which the corporation converts is organized, formed or created under the laws of a jurisdiction other than the State of Delaware`

-- What the certificate certifies: (1) the corporation's name and, if it has changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated; (2) the date of filing of its original certificate of
-- incorporation; (3) the name and jurisdiction of the entity; (4) that the conversion has been approved under the section; (5) its agreement that it may be served with process in Delaware (in an
-- action to enforce an obligation arising while it was a corporation of this State, or an obligation of the other entity arising from the conversion, including appraisal) and that it irrevocably
-- appoints the Secretary of State as its agent; (6) the address to which the Secretary of State is to mail a copy of the process; (7) if a plan of conversion is adopted under (l), that all its provisions
-- shall be approved in accordance with the section.
-- src:1354 | (1) The name of the corporation, and if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated;
-- src:1355 | (2) The date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State;
-- src:1356 | (3) The name and jurisdiction of the entity to which the corporation shall be converted;
-- src:1357 | (4) That the conversion has been approved in accordance with the provisions of this section;
-- src:1358 | (5) The agreement of the corporation that it may be served with process in the State of Delaware in any action, suit or proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the corporation arising while it was a corporation of this State, as well as for enforcement of any obligation of such other entity arising from the conversion, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262 of this title, and that it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such action, suit or proceeding; and
-- src:1359 | (6) The address to which a copy of the process referred to in paragraph (c)(5) of this section shall be mailed to it by the Secretary of State. Process may be served upon the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (c)(5) of this section by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. The Secretary of State is authorized to issue such rules and regulations with respect to such service as the Secretary of State deems necessary or appropriate. In the event of such service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (c)(5) of this section, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify such corporation that has converted out of the State of Delaware by letter, directed to such corporation that has converted out of the State of Delaware at the address so specified, unless such corporation shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address designated. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour service was made. The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
-- src:1360 | (7) If a plan of conversion is adopted in accordance with subsection (l) of this section, that all provisions of the plan of conversion shall be approved in accordance with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c) (src:1354-1360)
DECLARE `s 266(c) Certifications in the certificate of conversion` HAS
    `s 266(c)(1) the certificate certifies the name of the corporation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(1) the certificate certifies the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(2) the certificate certifies the date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(3) the certificate certifies the name and jurisdiction of the entity to which the corporation shall be converted`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(4) the certificate certifies that the conversion has been approved in accordance with the provisions of the section`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(5) the certificate certifies the agreement of the corporation that it may be served with process in the State of Delaware in any action, suit or proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the corporation arising while it was a corporation of this State or of any obligation of the other entity arising from the conversion, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(5) the certificate certifies that the corporation irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such action, suit or proceeding`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(6) the certificate certifies the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed to the corporation by the Secretary of State`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 266(c)(7) the certificate certifies that all provisions of the plan of conversion shall be approved in accordance with the section`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c) (src:1353-1360)
GIVEN `the name of the corporation has been changed since it was originally incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a plan of conversion is adopted in accordance with subsection (l)` IS A BOOLEAN
      certifications IS A `s 266(c) Certifications in the certificate of conversion`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 266(c) the certificate of conversion certifies what the subsection requires` MEANS
        certifications's `s 266(c)(1) the certificate certifies the name of the corporation`
    -- (1) "and if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated"
    AND (   (NOT `the name of the corporation has been changed since it was originally incorporated`)
         OR certifications's `s 266(c)(1) the certificate certifies the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated`)
    AND certifications's `s 266(c)(2) the certificate certifies the date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State`
    AND certifications's `s 266(c)(3) the certificate certifies the name and jurisdiction of the entity to which the corporation shall be converted`
    AND certifications's `s 266(c)(4) the certificate certifies that the conversion has been approved in accordance with the provisions of the section`
    AND certifications's `s 266(c)(5) the certificate certifies the agreement of the corporation that it may be served with process in the State of Delaware in any action, suit or proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the corporation arising while it was a corporation of this State or of any obligation of the other entity arising from the conversion, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262`
    AND certifications's `s 266(c)(5) the certificate certifies that the corporation irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such action, suit or proceeding`
    AND certifications's `s 266(c)(6) the certificate certifies the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed to the corporation by the Secretary of State`
    -- (7) "If a plan of conversion is adopted in accordance with subsection (l)"
    AND (   (NOT `a plan of conversion is adopted in accordance with subsection (l)`)
         OR certifications's `s 266(c)(7) the certificate certifies that all provisions of the plan of conversion shall be approved in accordance with the section`)

